# Test: Config reload REMOVES a capability the peer never used, and the session
#       still restarts -- because a second field moves with it.
# Initial config: peer1 declares capability extended-message enable
# After SIGHUP:   the extended-message line is gone; nothing else in the file differs
# Expected: the peer restarts, and the log names BOTH fields that forced it.
#
# VALIDATES: the boundary of the owner's ruling of 2026-08-07 -- "if capabilities
#            are removed from the peer which were not used ... we can accept the
#            change and keep the BGP session up, otherwise have to re-start and
#            re-negotiate". ze-peer mirrors ze's OPEN, so the peer DID advertise
#            extended-message here and the negotiation genuinely changes. The
#            capability half of the verdict is therefore restart on its own merits.
#            The second name in the log is the finding: parseCapabilitiesFromTree
#            (config_capabilities.go) also rewrites CapabilityConfigJSON, the blob
#            that carries the capability block to plugins, from the SAME edit.
#            negotiationOutcomeUnchanged (peer_settings_negotiation.go) cannot see
#            what a plugin would inject once it received that blob, so the field
#            restarts and no capability-block edit can reach the swap branch today.
# PREVENTS:  the restart reason naming one field when two forced it. An operator
#            who reads "Capabilities", makes the capability set negotiate
#            identically, and reloads again would watch the session flap a second
#            time for the field nobody told them about.
#
# DISCRIMINATION: the assertion is the exact reason STRING, not the presence of a
# restart. Returning early after the first changed field -- which the code did
# until 2026-08-07 -- still restarts, still logs "peer restart required", and
# fails this test on the reason alone. Deleting the log line fails it too.
#
# The swap branch of the ruling is proved where the config surface can reach it:
# TestNegotiationOutcomeDecidesSwapOrRestart and
# TestReloadCapabilityChangeKeepsTheSessionWhenNegotiationIsUnchanged
# (internal/component/bgp/reactor/peer_settings_negotiation_test.go) drive a real
# Reload() over a peer with a live negotiated session.

option=env:var=ze.log.bgp.reactor:value=debug

# ze-peer expectations
stdin=peer:terminator=EOF_PEER
option=tcp_connections:value=2

# Connection 1: Static route (192.168.1.0/24) + EOR
expect=bgp:conn=1:seq=1:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF00300200000015400101004002004003040A0000014005040000006418C0A801
expect=bgp:conn=1:seq=1:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF00170200000000

# After initial messages: drop the extended-message capability and SIGHUP.
action=rewrite:conn=1:seq=2:source=config2.conf:dest=ze-bgp.conf
action=sighup:conn=1:seq=2

# Connection 2: the restart reconnects and resends the same route.
expect=bgp:conn=2:seq=1:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF00300200000015400101004002004003040A0000014005040000006418C0A801
expect=bgp:conn=2:seq=1:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF00170200000000
EOF_PEER

# Initial ze bgp configuration: extended-message advertised
stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
bgp {
	peer peer1 {
		connection {
			remote {
				ip 127.0.0.1
			}
			local {
				ip 127.0.0.1
				accept false
			}
		}
		session {
			asn {
				local 1
				remote 1
			}
			router-id 1.2.3.4
			family {
				ipv4/unicast { prefix { maximum 10000; } }
			}
			capability {
				graceful-restart disable
				extended-message enable
			}
		}
		behavior {
			group-updates disable
		}

		update {
			attribute {
				origin igp
				local-preference 100
				next-hop 10.0.0.1
			}
			nlri {
				ipv4/unicast add 192.168.1.0/24
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

# Rewritten config: extended-message is gone; nothing else differs.
tmpfs=config2.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF2
bgp {
	peer peer1 {
		connection {
			remote {
				ip 127.0.0.1
			}
			local {
				ip 127.0.0.1
				accept false
			}
		}
		session {
			asn {
				local 1
				remote 1
			}
			router-id 1.2.3.4
			family {
				ipv4/unicast { prefix { maximum 10000; } }
			}
			capability {
				graceful-restart disable
			}
		}
		behavior {
			group-updates disable
		}

		update {
			attribute {
				origin igp
				local-preference 100
				next-hop 10.0.0.1
			}
			nlri {
				ipv4/unicast add 192.168.1.0/24
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF2

# Process orchestration
cmd=background:seq=1:exec=ze-peer --port $PORT:stdin=peer
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp:timeout=20s

# The restart names every field that forced it, in struct order after Capabilities.
expect=stderr:pattern=peer restart required
expect=stderr:pattern=changed=Capabilities,CapabilityConfigJSON
reject=stderr:pattern=peer settings swapped in place
